# Project Conventions

This is a Vue 3 + TypeScript prototype template using the AlayaCare Design System.

## Tech Stack

- **Vue 3** with `<script setup lang="ts">` (Composition API)
- **TypeScript** (strict mode with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`)
- **Vite** as build tool
- **Vue Router** for routing (`src/router/index.ts`)
- **Pinia** for state management (`src/stores/`)
- **MSW** (Mock Service Worker) for API mocking in development
- **@alayacare/alaya-design-system** for all UI components

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── assets/          # CSS and static assets
├── components/      # Reusable components
├── mocks/           # MSW handlers for API mocking
│   ├── browser.ts   # Worker setup
│   └── handlers.ts  # Request handlers
├── router/          # Vue Router config
│   └── index.ts
├── stores/          # Pinia stores
├── views/           # Route-level page components
├── App.vue          # Root layout with <RouterView />
└── main.ts          # App bootstrap
```

## Key Conventions

- Use `@/` path alias to import from `src/` (e.g., `import Foo from '@/components/Foo.vue'`)
- All components use `<script setup lang="ts">` syntax
- Page-level components go in `src/views/`, reusable components in `src/components/`
- Always prefer Alaya Design System (`Ac`-prefixed) components over raw HTML elements
- This project has no real backend — MSW runs in all environments as the API layer
- Add mock API handlers in `src/mocks/handlers.ts`; never gate MSW behind a DEV check
